    "title": "2,000 U.S. Troops From 82nd Airborne Division to Be Sent to Middle East",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTAround 2,000 U.S. Paratroopers to Be Sent to the Middle EastThe order gives President Trump more military options as he considers diplomacy with Iran. It is unclear where the soldiers will go in the Middle East.Listen · 2:53 min Members of the 82nd Airborne Division in North Carolina in 2021. It is unclear where roughly 2,000 soldiers from the division will go in the Middle East, but the location would be within striking distance of Iran, officials said.Credit...Getty ImagesMarch 24, 2026The Pentagon has ordered about 2,000 soldiers from the Army’s 82nd Airborne Division to begin moving to the Middle East to give President Trump additional military options even as he weighs a new diplomatic initiative with Iran, two Defense Department officials said on Tuesday.The combat forces would come from the division’s “Immediate Response Force,” a brigade of about 3,000 soldiers capable of deploying anywhere in the world within 18 hours.The contingent includes Maj. Gen. Brandon R. Tegtmeier, the division commander, and dozens of his staff members, as well as two battalions, each with about 800 soldiers, said the officials, who spoke on condition of anonymity to discuss operational matters. More of the brigade’s soldiers could be sent in the coming days, the officials said.Subscribe to The Times to read as many articles as you like.Eric Schmitt is a national security correspondent for The Times. He has reported on U.S. military affairs and counterterrorism for more than three decades.AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
